const e="usa-dance-varsity-nationals",d=2026,o="Built from the organiser's 2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations (Version 6.10), read in full. The rules print dates, deadlines and one contact address for Nationals; they do not print entry fee amounts, per-category marks, score sheets, the division sheet (division names by team size, Recreational birth years) or ages. The first 'Registration' paragraph says December 31st and the Deadlines list says December 23, 2025; the newer Deadlines list is used. The paragraph prints 'February 6, 2025' for first payment, kept as printed in the variable.",n=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"2025-26 USA Dance Regionals, Classics and High School Dance Nationals (United States)","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"Nationals registration closes {{NationalsRegistrationDeadline}}. Deposit {{DepositAmount}} per competitor by {{DepositDeadline}}; final balance {{FinalBalanceDeadline}}.","Notes":["Bids to Nationals: 80% of total possible points in Championship divisions, 75% in other team divisions.","Team routines are up to 3 minutes; solos up to 2 minutes."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["Event types: Regionals are one-day local qualifying competitions that no prior qualification is needed to enter; all performers receive a participation ribbon or other commemorative item and regional awards go to top teams in each division.","Classics are one-day events with no prior qualification needed. All performers receive a commemorative participation gift, trophies or plaques go to 50% of the teams in each division and each first place competitor receives an exclusive Champion event pin.","Not all divisions are offered at every Regional or Classic competition.","USA High School Dance Nationals began in 1986 and needs prior qualification. Specialty awards include Judges Award of Excellence, Best Choreography, Sweepstakes Style Awards and Grand Champion.","Team levels are Championship (no technical skill restrictions except the dance safety rules) and Intermediate (technical skill restrictions apply).","The competition director may cancel, combine or divide divisions as deemed necessary. If divisions are sub-divided, the number of awards is adjusted.","To be considered for the Nationals Grand Champion title, a team must compete at least one routine in Dance/Pom, Kick, Prop, Musical Theater and/or Hip Hop divisions.","A team must compete at Nationals in the same category and division it qualified in at a Regional or Classic, unless it has prior written approval. For example, a team that qualified for Hip Hop Championship may not compete in Hip Hop Intermediate at Nationals unless it also qualified for that category.","A team that qualifies for Nationals two or more times at the Championship level in Regionals or Classics must compete at the Championship level at Nationals.","Information is subject to change; the organiser asks teams to check its website for the latest competition information. The rules are the property of the organiser and may not be reproduced for events it does not sponsor or approve."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["At the time of competition, entrants must be registered students in the school they represent and official full-time members of their team.","High school teams: no member may be younger than 9th grade or older than 12th grade.","Jr High teams: no member may be older than 9th grade.","The penalty for an eligibility violation is disqualification of the routine.","A school may enter multiple teams (for example Drill Team and Dance Team, or JV and Varsity) as long as no individual competes on both teams. A dancer who is on two teams makes those teams share the 7-routine maximum.","An individual may not compete against herself or himself in the same division or category (for example in two X-Small Dance routines).","A team may compete in a JV division only if the school has a separate JV and Varsity team. No dancer (including alternates) may cross over between the Varsity and JV team, and the two teams may not combine in any category.","JV teams may not enter Varsity categories (Small, Medium and Large Dance, Hip Hop, Dance/Pom or Jazz) that are already offered as separate JV divisions. In categories without a JV division (for example Kick and Novelty), a JV team may compete in the Varsity category as a JV team.","At Nationals, 75% of the team competing must complete the Varsity Spirit/NFHS Squad Credentialing Program (new for 2025-26 in all divisions).","Coaches, directors, choreographers and personnel who wish to enter the warm-up area, backstage, coaches' box or athlete areas must have the credentialing, background check and safeguarding required by each event.","Co-Ed Dance teams must have at least 2 males and 2 females. All-Male Dance teams must be all males. These are the only divisions with male/female restrictions.","Recreational divisions: athlete eligibility is by birth year (or part year) listed for each division on the organiser's division sheet. Teams submit a Varsity Recreational Roster Verification Form at each event. All coaches need a USA Cheer Membership, and at least one coach with the USA Cheer Coach membership that includes the Youth Safety Risk Management course must accompany the team at every competition, with proof at registration.","For 2025-26, Recreational divisions are offered at Regionals only and are not eligible for USA Dance Nationals or USA Spirit Nationals. Recreational teams follow the same routine safety rules."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Nationals registration is online at the organiser's myVarsity account and must be submitted on or before {{NationalsRegistrationDeadline}}. Teams do not need to wait to qualify before registering, because registration closes before all Regionals have taken place.","Prior qualification through a USA Regional or Classic or another sanctioned event is required to enter Nationals in any division, except solos and Jr High teams. If there is no Regional or Classic in your area, the team must attend a virtual regional.","Performance order is set by registration date if the deposit or payment in full is received by the deposit due date. If it is not, the order is set by the date payment is received. The order may change for event flow, costume change needs and similar reasons.","Registrations are not confirmed until payment is received. Even with payment, entry is not guaranteed because the competition may close before the deadlines when it reaches capacity.","Registrations that are not paid in full or guaranteed by a school purchase order may be cancelled at any time, and are cancelled no later than {{FinalBalanceDeadline}}.","Deposit and paperwork deadline: {{DepositDeadline}}. Digital waivers deadline: {{WaiverDeadline}}. Division and roster change deadline: {{ChangeDeadline}}; there are no division or soloist name changes after that date.","For a legality review before the event, email a clear, close-up MP4 video of the skill (not the whole routine) with the school name and division to the organiser's dance rules address. Music and questionable lyrics can also be reviewed. For one-day events the video must be sent 14 days or more before the competition. A review does not stop a penalty at the event and does not guarantee a review.","The organiser's competition office can be contacted for registration questions ({{CompetitionsContact}})."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees and Payment","Items":["A deposit of {{DepositAmount}} per competitor is due with the additional paperwork by {{DepositDeadline}}. No other money is due until {{FirstPaymentDate}}.","The final balance is due {{FinalBalanceDeadline}}.","Accepted payment: school purchase order, school check, cashier's check, money order or credit card. Personal checks, organizational checks, cash and individual payments are not accepted. A purchase order must show the school name and an authorized signature. If a purchase order is used, the balance is due no later than 30 days after the event.","The rules do not print entry fee amounts per division."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates","Items":["USA Dance Nationals: {{NationalsDates}} at {{NationalsVenue}}.","Tentative Nationals schedule: Friday - Solo Champion prelims and semi-finals, and Senior, Junior and Sophomore/Freshman Solo divisions (prelims and finals); Saturday - team division prelims; Sunday - team division finals and Solo Champion finals."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Points, Bids and Deductions","Items":["Bids to Nationals go to teams that receive 80% of total possible points in all Championship divisions and 75% of total possible points in all other team divisions, regardless of any penalties received.","Deductions (points): number of performers over or under the division size limit 0.50 per occurrence; Intermediate skill restriction violation 2.0 per occurrence; entrance/exit over 30 seconds (group divisions) 0.1 per second; Prop and Musical Theater entrance/exit over 1.5 minutes 0.10 per second; routine over the time limit 0.1 per second; equipment dropped 0.50 per occurrence (includes pom drops in Dance/Pom).","Inappropriate music/lyrics, appearance or movements 3.0; illegal tumbling, prop dismount or lifts 3.0 (includes touching down a non hands-free pom on tumbling); illegal prop restriction 10.0 (a prop that breaks the safety rules or is used outside the Prop and Musical Theater divisions, not including hand-held props); unnecessary change in performance order 2.0.","The score sheets are on the organiser's rules and scoring web page. Marks per criterion are not printed in the rules document."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Recognition","Items":["Regionals: participation ribbon or commemorative item for all performers, and awards for top teams in each division.","Classics: commemorative participation gift, trophies or plaques for 50% of the teams in each division, a Champion event pin for each first place competitor, and sponsor give-aways at selected events.","Nationals: Judges Award of Excellence, Best Choreography, Sweepstakes Style Awards and Grand Champion. Scholarships, Championship backpacks, banners and medallions are mentioned as available."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Entry Limits","Items":["At Regionals and Classics a high school can compete 7 routines per team and 3 solos per school unless otherwise noted.","At Nationals a high school can compete 7 routines per team and 5 soloists. If the school has a JV team, up to 7 additional team performances are allowed for the JV team.","A soloist from any team may compete only one solo per USA event.","A team that has the same dancer on two teams must share the 7 routines between them."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Time, Props, Music and Safety","Items":["Time limit: all team divisions up to 3 minutes per routine (Dance, Contemporary, Military, Hip Hop, Jazz, Lyrical, Kick, Dance/Drill, Co-Ed, All-Male, Dance/Pom, Prop and Musical Theater). Timing starts at the first note of music or movement and ends at the last note or movement.","Entrance and exit: up to 30 seconds each for all Dance, Contemporary, Military, Hip Hop, Jazz, Lyrical, Kick, Dance/Drill, Co-Ed, All-Male and Dance/Pom divisions; up to 1.5 minutes each for Prop and Musical Theater. Timing starts when the team is announced or at the first sign of movement to enter, whichever is first.","All routine choreography, movements and costuming must suit a family friendly environment and an audience of all ages. Movements implying something indecent, offensive or sexual are not allowed.","Music may not contain inappropriate words, phrases or sounds in any language: references to consuming alcohol, pejorative words, illegal activities for minors, violence or inciting violence, sexual references or offensive language about any group. The coach is responsible for screening all music. Each infraction of inappropriate music, costuming or movement is a 3-point penalty.","Shoes are not required. Shoes worn must have soft, non-marking soles; marking the floor is disqualification and the school pays for floor damage. Dancers without shoes perform at their own risk. Shoes are required at all other times when not performing.","Costuming must be well secured and appropriate. Jewelry and accessories are allowed if secured to the dancer.","Hand-held and wearable props (for example ball, box or scarf, used and carried by an individual dancer) are allowed in all divisions, but a hand-held prop that can bear the full weight of one or more dancers is not.","Sets and backdrops are allowed only in the Prop and Musical Theater divisions. They are not allowed in Dance, Contemporary, Lyrical, Hip Hop, Kick, Dance/Drill, Co-Ed, Military, Solo, Dance/Pom and All-Male.","All props must be non-marking, with padding or rubber wheels. The penalty is disqualification, and the school pays for floor damage.","Props, sets and accessories must fit through a standard door 7 feet high by 63 inches wide. During the entrance or exit time a team may assemble props to any size, but all assembly must fit in the time allowed. Assembly before the entrance time and before entering the gym is allowed only if the assembled prop still meets the door size. All teams must enter and exit with all props at the time of performance; props may not be stored in the venue unless the competition information says so. The penalty is 10 points per prop infraction.","If a prop, set or accessory stands higher than 4 feet from the floor, a dancer may jump, tumble or fall from it only at 4 feet or below. Competition directors may measure assembled props.","Lifts: a horizontal lift or an upside-down lift is legal if the bases keep direct contact with the lifted dancer above head level and at least one base keeps contact with the head, neck or upper body of the lifted dancer. Standing or stepping on another dancer's torso is legal if the lifted dancer is physically supported by at least one other dancer. Elevators, thigh stands, chair sits and shoulder sits are allowed.","Not allowed, with routine disqualification: extended cheer stunts (lifted dancer upright over bases with fully extended arms), pyramids and basket tosses.","Tumbling: front tucks, back tucks (including toe pitch back tucks) and layouts are not allowed. Airborne skills may not jump from a standing or squatting position backwards onto the neck, back or shoulders. A kip-up motion must start with the back or shoulder area touching the ground (this rule applies to the rubber band or bronco kip-up only).","Non hands-free poms used for aerial cartwheels must be moved to one hand; if both poms are not moved to one hand or the hand holding both poms touches down, there is a 3-point penalty. Hands-free poms are allowed: an elastic band only between the supporting hand and the floor, bars not in the palm. A hair tie, rubber band or tied pom strings do not count as hands-free poms.","Participants, coaches, gym owners, directors and spectators must follow the organiser's Code of Conduct and prohibited items list for all Regional, Virtual and Championship events. Event guidelines (general, safety, music, interruption of performance, competition area, warm-up room) and event policies are on the organiser's website.","Intermediate division skill restrictions: dancers must have 2 counts between completing one technical skill and starting another (exceptions: chaines and piques in succession, chaine battement/fan and chaine jete/calypso leaps). Leg work and extensions count as technical skills.","Intermediate turns: single and double pirouettes may be in passe, coupe, pencil and attitude positions; a single or double pirouette with a plie into a single turn is allowed. A maximum of two separate turn sequences is allowed, each limited to fouette turns, a la seconde turns and pirouettes within one 8-count of turning, not consecutive, with consistent spot direction, no touching the working leg and no floats. Traveling turns and separate pirouettes are not turn sequences.","Intermediate leaps and jumps: switch and scissor leaps are not allowed; leaps and jumps cannot connect to another skill; preparation is limited to a step or chasse (chaine turn as preparation is not allowed except chaine jete or calypso leap); head release to the back is allowed. Permitted examples: double pirouettes, single leg hold turn, side somis, center leap, turning disc, one 8-count of fouette or second turns, chaine jete or calypso leap, kip-ups. Not permitted examples: triple pirouettes or more, double leg hold turns or more, tour jete, axels, surprise leap, switch or scissor leap, reverse leap, turn sequences longer than one 8-count, 3 or more turn sequences, toe touch, floats, aerials, butterflies, headsprings with hands, multiple jump sequences, tilt jump. The organiser decides skills not listed by comparison.","Intermediate exception (Regionals and the March 2026 Nationals only): up to 2 'spotlights' of at most one 8-count each are allowed in a routine, with 3 or fewer dancers spotlighted at one time. A spotlight starts at the first count where the dancer goes beyond the Intermediate restrictions."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Questions","Items":["Questions about the safety rules or division restrictions can be sent to the organiser's dance rules address; see the legality review steps under How to Register."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other Parts of the Rules","Items":["Competition types: Regionals, Classics and High School Dance Nationals are described under General Rules. Dance Nationals teams may be from the western United States and beyond.","Recreational, Jr High, team-size (Small, Medium, Large) and Novelty divisions are mentioned in the rules, but the full division list is on the organiser's separate 2025-26 division sheet and is not part of this template.","Solo competition guidelines are listed as coming soon on the organiser's website; the solo rules here come from the Individual Solo Competition section."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations (PDF)","Url":"https://varsity.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/2025-26-USA-Dance-Rules-Regulations-1.pdf"}]}`),t=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Individual Solo Competition",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Solo routine: up to 2 minutes, with an entrance of up to 15 seconds and an exit of up to 15 seconds."],Rules:["Any dance style or combination of styles may be used.","A soloist from any team may compete only one solo per USA event.","Nationals solo divisions: Solo Champion, Senior, Junior and Sophomore/Freshman. A school may enter 1 Solo Champion, 1 Senior, 1 Junior and up to 1 Sophomore and 1 Freshman dancer.","Nationals schedule: Solo Champion prelims and semi-finals and the Senior, Junior and Sophomore/Freshman solo prelims and finals on the first day; Solo Champion finals on the last day."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Solo routine: up to 2 minutes, with an entrance of up to 15 seconds and an exit of up to 15 seconds.

## Rules
- Any dance style or combination of styles may be used.
- A soloist from any team may compete only one solo per USA event.
- Nationals solo divisions: Solo Champion, Senior, Junior and Sophomore/Freshman. A school may enter 1 Solo Champion, 1 Senior, 1 Junior and up to 1 Sophomore and 1 Freshman dancer.
- Nationals schedule: Solo Champion prelims and semi-finals and the Senior, Junior and Sophomore/Freshman solo prelims and finals on the first day; Solo Champion finals on the last day.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Guidelines, Time Limitations",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Team routine: up to 3 minutes. Entrance and exit up to 30 seconds each (1.5 minutes each for Prop and Musical Theater)."],Rules:["A school may enter 7 routines per team at Regionals, Classics and Nationals.","A team that does not have the number of performers the division requires gets a 0.50 deduction per occurrence."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Team routine: up to 3 minutes. Entrance and exit up to 30 seconds each (1.5 minutes each for Prop and Musical Theater).

## Rules
- A school may enter 7 routines per team at Regionals, Classics and Nationals.
- A team that does not have the number of performers the division requires gets a 0.50 deduction per occurrence.`}],a=[{AgeGroup:"Varsity Championship",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Championship Division Limitations",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Championship level: no technical skill restrictions except the dance safety rules.","Bids to Nationals need 80% of total possible points. A team that earns two or more bids at Championship level must compete at Championship level at Nationals."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Championship level: no technical skill restrictions except the dance safety rules.
- Bids to Nationals need 80% of total possible points. A team that earns two or more bids at Championship level must compete at Championship level at Nationals.`},{AgeGroup:"Varsity Intermediate",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Intermediate Division Skill Restrictions",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Intermediate level: the Intermediate skill restrictions apply; a violation is a 2.0 deduction per occurrence.","Bids to Nationals need 75% of total possible points."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Intermediate level: the Intermediate skill restrictions apply; a violation is a 2.0 deduction per occurrence.
- Bids to Nationals need 75% of total possible points.`},{AgeGroup:"JV Teams",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Only for a school that has a separate JV and Varsity team; no dancer may cross over between them.","JV divisions printed: JV Dance, JV Hip Hop, JV Dance/Pom and JV Jazz. In categories with no JV division, such as Kick, a JV team competes in the Varsity category as a JV team.","At Nationals a JV team may add up to 7 team performances."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Only for a school that has a separate JV and Varsity team; no dancer may cross over between them.
- JV divisions printed: JV Dance, JV Hip Hop, JV Dance/Pom and JV Jazz. In categories with no JV division, such as Kick, a JV team competes in the Varsity category as a JV team.
- At Nationals a JV team may add up to 7 team performances.`},{AgeGroup:"Dance Showcase Teams",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Evaluation only: routines are rated against the organiser's score sheet for an overall rating based on scoring.","Offered at Regionals and Classics only."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Evaluation only: routines are rated against the organiser's score sheet for an overall rating based on scoring.
- Offered at Regionals and Classics only.`},{AgeGroup:"Sophomore-Freshman Solo",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Up to 1 Sophomore and 1 Freshman dancer per school in this solo division at Nationals."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Up to 1 Sophomore and 1 Freshman dancer per school in this solo division at Nationals.`},{AgeGroup:"Junior Solo",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["1 Junior dancer per school at Nationals."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 1 Junior dancer per school at Nationals.`},{AgeGroup:"Senior Solo",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["1 Senior dancer per school at Nationals."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 1 Senior dancer per school at Nationals.`},{AgeGroup:"Solo Champion",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Guidelines",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["1 Solo Champion per school at Nationals. Solo Champion prelims and semi-finals are on the first day and finals on the last day."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- 1 Solo Champion per school at Nationals. Solo Champion prelims and semi-finals are on the first day and finals on the last day.`}],i=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Dance","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":["The overall effect must be dance in nature. Any dance style or combination of styles is acceptable. Dance attire or school uniforms may be used."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The overall effect must be dance in nature. Any dance style or combination of styles is acceptable. Dance attire or school uniforms may be used."},{"Title":"Contemporary","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":["Movement emphasizes use of space, body awareness, a variety of movement qualities, gestural motions and possible motifs (for example suspension, off-center movement, momentum and gravity). It expresses movement through the whole body and does not follow strict ballet or jazz forms."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Movement emphasizes use of space, body awareness, a variety of movement qualities, gestural motions and possible motifs (for example suspension, off-center movement, momentum and gravity). It expresses movement through the whole body and does not follow strict ballet or jazz forms."},{"Title":"Dance Showcase","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":["For any performing arts program or team to gain performance experience for evaluation only. Performances are evaluated against the USA score sheet for an overall rating based on scoring. Any dance style or combination of styles is acceptable. Offered at Regionals and Classics only."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- For any performing arts program or team to gain performance experience for evaluation only. Performances are evaluated against the USA score sheet for an overall rating based on scoring. Any dance style or combination of styles is acceptable. Offered at Regionals and Classics only."},{"Title":"Co-Ed Dance","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The team must have at least 2 males and 2 females.","Any dance style or combination of styles. Partnering interactions must be the emphasis for at least 50% of the routine."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The team must have at least 2 males and 2 females.\\n- Any dance style or combination of styles. Partnering interactions must be the emphasis for at least 50% of the routine."},{"Title":"All-Men Dance","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions (All-Male Dance)","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The team must be all males. Any dance style or combination of styles."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The team must be all males. Any dance style or combination of styles."},{"Title":"Lyrical","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":["All dancers interpret the lyrics, mood or intent of a song (with or without words) using ballet, jazz and/or modern technique. Movement uses the music or lyrics as a guide. Balance and sustained movement, and facial and body emotion, are expected."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- All dancers interpret the lyrics, mood or intent of a song (with or without words) using ballet, jazz and/or modern technique. Movement uses the music or lyrics as a guide. Balance and sustained movement, and facial and body emotion, are expected."},{"Title":"Dance/Pom","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The emphasis must be on the use of pom, with visual staging and complex pom movement.","Teams must use two poms for at least three-fourths of the routine.","Standard school uniforms, dance or military clothing may be worn."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The emphasis must be on the use of pom, with visual staging and complex pom movement.\\n- Teams must use two poms for at least three-fourths of the routine.\\n- Standard school uniforms, dance or military clothing may be worn."},{"Title":"Hip Hop","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":["Dancers perform a variety of street style movements that show the artistry and technique of hip hop or styles that evolved in hip-hop culture. Difficulty is shown through body awareness and muscle control, textures, dynamics and variety of hip hop styles (for example vogue, locking, breaking, popping, whacking, house). Any genre of music may be used if the routine as a whole is hip hop style."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Dancers perform a variety of street style movements that show the artistry and technique of hip hop or styles that evolved in hip-hop culture. Difficulty is shown through body awareness and muscle control, textures, dynamics and variety of hip hop styles (for example vogue, locking, breaking, popping, whacking, house). Any genre of music may be used if the routine as a whole is hip hop style."},{"Title":"Military","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The routine must be military in nature, with precision and sharpness through the whole body, military maneuvers, pattern formations, visual effects, arm and hand sequences and a variety of marching styles (glide, high knee, prance, pony, chug and similar).","School uniforms or military attire must be worn. All maneuvering, marching and traveling must begin on the left foot. All difficulty and technical elements must keep military style."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The routine must be military in nature, with precision and sharpness through the whole body, military maneuvers, pattern formations, visual effects, arm and hand sequences and a variety of marching styles (glide, high knee, prance, pony, chug and similar).\\n- School uniforms or military attire must be worn. All maneuvering, marching and traveling must begin on the left foot. All difficulty and technical elements must keep military style."},{"Title":"Dance/Drill","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The routine combines the Military and Dance guidelines: half dance and half military movement, with neither style emphasized over the other."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The routine combines the Military and Dance guidelines: half dance and half military movement, with neither style emphasized over the other."},{"Title":"Kick","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Kicks must be the focal point and used for more than three-fourths of the total routine length. Any style of movement may be used.","The routine must include a variety of kick sequences and kick types."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Kicks must be the focal point and used for more than three-fourths of the total routine length. Any style of movement may be used.\\n- The routine must include a variety of kick sequences and kick types."},{"Title":"Jazz","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":["The routine is rooted in the broad spectrum of jazz dance, using vocabulary from any jazz technique (theatrical, vernacular, technical, stylized, classical/concert, pop and others). Choreography should show the jazz foundation: bold dramatic movement, isolations, contractions, rhythm, musicality, energy, expression and dynamics."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The routine is rooted in the broad spectrum of jazz dance, using vocabulary from any jazz technique (theatrical, vernacular, technical, stylized, classical/concert, pop and others). Choreography should show the jazz foundation: bold dramatic movement, isolations, contractions, rhythm, musicality, energy, expression and dynamics."},{"Title":"Prop","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The creative and visual use of a prop or props must be the emphasis, and handling the prop must be the focal point rather than the dancer's movement. The prop must be used in at least three-fourths of the routine.","Any style of dance may be used. Theme in the routine or uniform is allowed but must not be the focal point. Standard school uniforms or costumes may be worn.","Sets and backdrops are allowed. Entrance and exit up to 1.5 minutes each."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The creative and visual use of a prop or props must be the emphasis, and handling the prop must be the focal point rather than the dancer's movement. The prop must be used in at least three-fourths of the routine.\\n- Any style of dance may be used. Theme in the routine or uniform is allowed but must not be the focal point. Standard school uniforms or costumes may be worn.\\n- Sets and backdrops are allowed. Entrance and exit up to 1.5 minutes each."},{"Title":"Musical Theater","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Division Descriptions","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The routine must have a unique theme and emphasize a story line, character or musical theater concept that does not depend on the audience or judges knowing its origin.","Technical dance movement is allowed if it makes sense within the theme, character or story. Props are allowed but should only support the story. Themed costumes should be worn. Sets and backdrops are allowed but not required. Entrance and exit up to 1.5 minutes each."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The routine must have a unique theme and emphasize a story line, character or musical theater concept that does not depend on the audience or judges knowing its origin.\\n- Technical dance movement is allowed if it makes sense within the theme, character or story. Props are allowed but should only support the story. Themed costumes should be worn. Sets and backdrops are allowed but not required. Entrance and exit up to 1.5 minutes each."},{"Title":"Solo","Source":"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Individual Solo Competition","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":["Up to 2 minutes, entrance up to 15 seconds and exit up to 15 seconds."],"Rules":["Any dance style or combination of styles may be used."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["Sets and backdrops are not allowed in Solo."]},"Markdown":"## Time and format\\n- Up to 2 minutes, entrance up to 15 seconds and exit up to 15 seconds.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Any dance style or combination of styles may be used.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Sets and backdrops are not allowed in Solo."}]`),s=[],l=[{Key:"NationalsDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Nationals dates",Value:"2026-03-13 to 2026-03-15",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Save the Date"},{Key:"NationalsVenue",Kind:"address",Label:"Nationals venue",Value:{Name:"Anaheim Convention Center",Address:"",City:"Anaheim, CA",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Save the Date"},{Key:"NationalsRegistrationDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to register for Nationals",Value:"2025-12-23",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Deadlines (the Registration paragraph also says December 31st; the Deadlines list is newer and used)"},{Key:"DepositDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Deposit and paperwork deadline",Value:"2026-01-06",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Deadlines"},{Key:"DepositAmount",Kind:"fee",Label:"Deposit per competitor",Value:"USD 100",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Deadlines"},{Key:"FirstPaymentDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date when money is first due",Value:"2026-02-06 (printed as February 6, 2025)",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Registration"},{Key:"ChangeDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Division and roster change deadline",Value:"2026-02-23",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Deadlines"},{Key:"WaiverDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Digital waivers deadline",Value:"2026-02-19",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Deadlines"},{Key:"FinalBalanceDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Final balance due",Value:"2026-02-27",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Deadlines"},{Key:"CompetitionsContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Competition office",Value:{Name:"USA Competitions",Role:"Organiser competition office",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"USACompetitions@varsity.com"},Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations, Save the Date"}],r=[{Claim:"Rules, eligibility, deadlines, deductions, safety rules and division descriptions captured from the organiser's own 2025-26 rules.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"2025-26 USA Dance Rules and Regulations",Url:"https://varsity.com/usa/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/2025-26-USA-Dance-Rules-Regulations-1.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:o,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:t,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:l,Evidence:r};export{a as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,r as Evidence,o as Note,n as Page,t as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,l as Variables,d as Year,u as default};
